  "beforeYouRead": "They say faith can move mountains. But what should we put our faith in? This is the question this story delicately poses.\n\nLencho is a farmer who writes a letter to God when his crops are ruined, asking for a hundred pesos. Does Lencho’s letter reach God? Does God send him the money? Think what your answers to these questions would be, and guess how the story continues, before you begin to read it. 1.\n\nOne of the cheapest ways to send money to someone is through the post office. Have you ever sent or received money in this way?  Here’s what you have to do.  (As you read the instructions, discuss with your teacher in class the meanings of these words: counter, counter clerk, appropriate, acknowledgement, counterfoil, record. Consult a dictionary if necessary. Are there words corresponding to these English words in your languages?) 2.\n\nFill out the Money Order form given below using the clues that follow the form.",
